+# Performance history
+
+## UserPromptSubmit read path
+
+No measured p95 for the full-recall UserPromptSubmit hook against an adversarial
+30-word synthetic vocabulary was found in this project's own records (research
+logs, benchmark scripts/output, or source comments). A figure for this exact
+scenario (before a term-selection fix, and the fix itself) could not be located
+in `research/00-evidence-log.md`, `research/CONCLUSION.md`,
+`research/CONCLUSION-v1-superada.md`, or the `research/bench/` and
+`crates/muninn-bench/` benchmark code, so no number is recorded here rather
+than estimating one.
+
+The closest documented, source-backed measurements of the full hook path are
+in `research/00-evidence-log.md` [I3] and `research/CONCLUSION.md`:
+
+- Full hook, end-to-end (fork + exec + open SQLite + intent gate + BM25 top-8 +
+  output), 50,000-record index, turn with intent: p50 4.07 ms / p95 4.31 ms.
+- Same setup, turn without intent (gate short-circuits): p50 0.49 ms / p95 0.56 ms.
+
+These do not use an adversarial 30-word vocabulary and are not the number
+requested; they are included only as the nearest verified reference point.
+
+If a measurement for the adversarial 30-word vocabulary case exists, it should
+be added here with a citation to the file/line where it was recorded, and this
+note should be removed.
